Z||000000||Pike||10-10-2001||01:53 AM||||The book says EGR. All lines hooked up and no leaks...any ideas? Service engine light comes on and stays on.<BR>Thanks,<BR>Pike<P>PS. I guess it could be the EGR...but prolly not.||||reg||1
Z||000001||My7Fieros||10-10-2001||02:47 AM||||Well your EGR prob needs replaced then (not the EGR tube, that'd cause a high idle and throw an "idle air control" code (whatever that is, I dont have my book in front of me). You really cant tell if the EGR is bad or not by looking. You <I>may</I> be able to tell by feeling underneath it and pushing the little "thingy"  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> (sorry) and see if it pushes in and springs back...either way you prob outta replace the EGR.<P>------------------<BR><FONT SIZE="3"><FONT COLOR="blue"><B><I>My 7 Fieros</FONT></FONT></B></I>||||reg||1
Z||000002||Joe Torma||10-10-2001||09:31 AM||||Could be the EGR control solinoid above the water pump.||||reg||1
Z||000003||skitime||10-10-2001||10:23 AM||||  <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Joe Torma:<BR><B>Could be the EGR control solenoid above the water pump.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>I agree with Joe.  I had the same problem and Jelly2M8 advised me to change the solenoid. I did and the problem was fixed.<P>BTW Hi Joe<P>------------------<BR><UL TYPE=SQUARE><BR><LI>Red 88 GT T-TOP<BR><LI>Red 86 GT<BR></UL>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/signature-2.JPG">  <p>[This message has been edited by skitime (edited 10-10-2001).]||||reg||1
